###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The learning rate 0.1 is that of the final stochastic-gradient-descent stage, the only value stated; the Adam learning rate of the main stage is not given.
# - Table 3 (ablations of the four-layer network) and the appendix experiments on QM9 and on the Materials Project molecule data set are not encoded.
# - The materials applications (hydrocarbon geometries, lattice constants and cohesive energies of metals and semiconductors, amorphous SiO2, water, proton diffusion; Table 4 and figures) have no MetricProperty; that MD was run with the potential is clear from these sections, but the simulation code and conditions were not captured, so supportsSimulation is not asserted.
# - The plane-wave cutoff is given only through PREC = Medium and is not encoded as a number.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
